ref 17592186045417] [17592186132421 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1017a124-cd54-55e1-978b-fc33a296608e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132422 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132422 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132422 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "90f97415-4f07-5a8e-b35c-68c70c6f316f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132423 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132423 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132423 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9a709aa9-9771-5c50-8782-046301c300aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132424 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132424 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132424 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e8639077-266e-5e5f-88d0-49b030a181d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132425 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132425 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132425 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4309781f-ea0d-54a0-a9c4-99e52a0a7d5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132426 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132426 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132426 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45de60d6-379e-52b3-823e-46e93bfb190a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133552 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133552 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider ![](images/46/4632b2999b4578282c7f0d71fdf36004123551187fa9a6980051d7ff89f48296.svg) and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133552 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "126c85b8-d721-5e7d-a3dc-df997bc0b9ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133552 #edb/ref 1074 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation $R_2 :=R_2+7R_3$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186133553 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4733" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133553 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133553 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f8eb89c4-1cca-5f8c-909c-31e9e0fc8412" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133553 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2-2R_1$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/a2/a23e35f367c6d8ca4bdbee47bacf9afca23dea031b0a647dda5067746bf45e46.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186133554 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4734" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133554 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad\n\tR_1:=6R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133554 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e47a532-ba7a-5692-961b-eabc743d74e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133554 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/d2/d2425878812bb00748c5250dd877655a7d01faab33e148593be2a6c2de98ac4e.svg)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/c7/c741f5faf39a8bc1606d64e906162bbd5b67b3dfd88af2372f43e96736de6bb5.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186133552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133742 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921861