 17592186134605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133980 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133980 #edb/ref 1045 "Row Operations on 3x3 Matrices as Products of Elementary Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133980 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186134602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133980 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133980 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133980 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "50a0ef69-74ee-5204-af04-a18cf1e2ad62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134188 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186131167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134188 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134188 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n$R_{1}↔R_{3}, R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2R_{3}, R_{1}:=3R_{1}$\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134188 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "82b71e56-3d28-5ee4-abda-f6f05cdef408" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134190 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134190 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134190 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider $E=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186134190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "67780f7b-b335-51d6-8512-e61d1ae7ee4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134190 #edb/ref 1074 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the second rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186134397 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186132421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134397 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42538" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134397 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{3}, R_{2}:=-3R_{2}$\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134397 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1dbb1aa-689b-52a9-913e-1f549be5077b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134602 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134602 #edb/ref 1061 17243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134602 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fa6e7f35-addb-57cf-a360-9e6406254399" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134602 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186135024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134603 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134603 #edb/ref 1061 17244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134603 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2fd97122-b858-5040-a119-fad68a3d03fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134603 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134604 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134604 #edb/ref 1061 17245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134604 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "da013532-9009-5401-a121-9e5bc3920d43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134604 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134605 #edb/ref 1061 17246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ec9418ab-c448-5510-808b-5f8b1a2094a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135024 #edb/ref 1064 "Applying a row operation to any $3\\times 3$ matrix is the same as *pre-multiplying* (multiplying on the left) the matrix by the corresponding elementary matrix.\n\nFor instance, if we wish to swap the first row and the second row of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ we pre-multiply $A$ by the corresponding elementary matrix \n![](images/2d/2de2ee02cbd3b00b6945fc8df8d84e83920fc0889c76394c1c726c94d68b1d99.svg)\nto get $E_1 A.$\n\nTo perform a sequence of row operations to a $3\\times 3$ matrix, we pre-multiply the matrix by the elementary matrix corresponding to the first operation, and then pre-multiply the result by the elementary matrix corresponding to the second operation.\n\nFor instance, given a $3 \\times 3$ matrix $A,$ suppose that we would like to multiply the second row by $2$ and then add $3$ times the first row to the second row. To do this, we first pre-multiply $A$ by \n![](images/61/61f42ffa5ee0defeb3330421ead9c42f84200b274577c96cffe1d59ed9cf5cef.svg)\nto get $E_2 A.$ Then we pre-multiply the result by \n![](images/be/be5d3785649ca7ac1557b43ca434c2558af417d29db47c10ef2938c1099db6f5.svg) \nto get $E_3 E_2 A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135024 #edb/ref 1065 3171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135024 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c110a2ca-8856-5b26-9ded-2e9f35023747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135024 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244443 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186244443 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244443 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e7315f0-8f33-584d-a228-448a96c382a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245037 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186245037 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245037 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5170a4b6-2e55-540e-a9fb-a40ab98bfacd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245180 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186245180 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245180 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "63386325-897f-52d1-8442-84f7f16497fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246075 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186246075 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246075 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c6660e14-5917-559c-97e3-eef966c951d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246398 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186246398 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246398 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eaa611e1-a025-517c-9cfa-3a06d2c77cc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186244443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246684 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4f247efd-629d-577a-996e-abd12be61f0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247126 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247126 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110473" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247126 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247126 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{1}:=-2{R}_{1}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247126 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84958816-55f1-5458-85cd-81127d794879" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247126 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-2{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186299992 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186299992 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299992 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0bc404a6-d316-58c1-b56c-a595600e5fdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300017 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300017 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300017 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0f052266-a78d-53f6-a624-dbcfb60c6b7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300156 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300156 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300156 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28489d41-fcfe-5fbd-aa9f-58d8c03fdfa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300301 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300301 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300301 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "447d16d4-e4ed-5411-a267-a5cd72c6a62a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300375 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186300375 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300375 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4f27f1d5-de6e-5780-b1ae-07308f92edd5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300553 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300553 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300553 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "78150501-86d3-5ad2-b18d-3aa575407c19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300577 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186300577 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300577 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7bb1b90c-e720-592f-8ba9-f2f4f1bd0389" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300634 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186300634 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300634 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "85d6c1f1-b43e-5c0a-925c-0e868e7f0b14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301088 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186301088 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301088 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e2cac16f-758b-5dd9-b61a-f47b814cb964" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301110 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301110 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301110 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e840a680-6695-5b5e-b17d-1a0d7769e11b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186299992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186301088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301429 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3e346c9e-f73f-5c61-a8d0-3c774b70c08c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301965 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e8eef8d5-a521-5905-9cae-619b2505ad27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302051 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302051 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32133" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302051 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302051 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302051 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f41cbfea-5742-50ae-9cb7-b244cecfac9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302051 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186327258 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186327258 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327258 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "255b1ea2-ed27-596e-8626-b1b2d8321ddb" #